    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: f9a93c7bf85b621df49e157b90b894c0637ddf55 -->\n**Review of head `f9a93c7bf`: clean.** The coordinator read the diff: three rules with their comments in `.gitattributes`, in the form of the rules above them. No other file changes.\n\n- `AGENTS.md`: read by `xtask` `light_tests` and `heavy_plan_tests`.\n- `site/**/*.md`: read by `xtask` `catalog_links_tests` and `catalog_tests`.\n- `crates/post/tests/klartext/contour.cnc`: read by `script_heidenhain_klartext`.\n\nEvidence from the author's run (git commands only): each matched file is `i/lf` before the rule, so no blob is renormalised. A checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` gives `w/crlf` before the rule and `w/lf` with it, for one file of each tree.\n\nThe decision is in the PR body: targeted rules are taken; one global `* text=auto eol=lf` is dropped (seven `.rs` files hold real CR bytes); the reader of `docs_troubleshooting` is #3619.\n\nNo build ran: on an LF checkout the change has no effect. The merge waits for the post-merge run of `main` at `4dba7019d`.\n",
